## Configuration

Every invocation resolves configuration from, in precedence order: an
explicit `--param` override (never present at runtime — CLI-only), the
Lambda **event payload** (a top-level key matching a declared parameter's
name/alias overrides that parameter for this invocation), environment
variables, then declared defaults
([`docs/reference/core/script.md`](../../docs/reference/core/script.md)
"Configuration from the Lambda event"). Set environment variables on the
function itself (console, IaC); there is no `.env` file at runtime.

## Local development (`.env`)

For local testing only (the "Minimal" example above, or a unit test), a
`scripts/__SCRIPT_NAME__/.env` file works the same way it would for a CLI
script — gitignored, listed in `.worktreeinclude` so worktrees inherit it.
Secrets go **only** here or in config `secretNames` — never in source or
fixtures. Per-script data isolation (ADR-0022):

```dotenv
M3L_CONFIG_DIR=<absolute-repo-path>/data/__SCRIPT_NAME__/config
M3L_INPUT_DIR=<absolute-repo-path>/data/__SCRIPT_NAME__/input
M3L_OUTPUT_DIR=<absolute-repo-path>/data/__SCRIPT_NAME__/output
```

## Data directories

| Directory | Purpose                                          |
| --------- | ------------------------------------------------ |
| `config/` | Presets / config files used during local testing |
| `input/`  | Files the script consumes during local testing   |
| `output/` | Run results during local testing                 |
